Package: riabuild
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @DEB_ARCH@
Maintainer: Clubria <engineering@clubria.com>
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://riabuild.clubria.com
Depends: git
Recommends: libsecret-tools, xdg-utils, bash-completion
Description: Sets up a Clubria developer's machine and opens the Clubria environment
 riabuild gets a developer from "accepted a GitHub org invite" to "running
 Claude Code against the Clubria codebase with working secrets" without them
 making a single environment decision.
 .
 It keeps its state in ~/.riabuild and the session token in the system keyring.
 Node, pnpm, Claude Code, gh, and infisical are downloaded and verified by
 riabuild itself, so this package depends on almost nothing.
 .
 git is a hard dependency: riabuild reports on the checkout every time it runs.
 libsecret-tools provides secret-tool, which is where the session token lives —
 without it riabuild works only with RIABUILD_TOKEN set, which is the right
 answer on a headless box and the wrong one on a laptop. xdg-utils provides
 xdg-open, used once, to put the browser in front of the GitHub sign-in.
 bash-completion loads the completion file this package installs; zsh and fish
 need nothing extra, so it is a Recommends rather than a Depends.
